These examples use the vendor PF grammar documented in pf.conf(5).

pf.conf is an inactive, fully commented IPv4 gateway template. Adapt the
interface names, addresses and policy before installing any selected rules in
/etc/pf.conf. A block/pass policy in an example does not change the kernel's
unmatched default, and installing this examples package does not enable PF.
Run pfctl -nf /path/to/proposed.conf before loading a real configuration.

The historical faq-example*, ackpri, queue* and spamd files used retired
ALTQ or pre-match NAT/redirection syntax. They are no longer installed as
current examples. Consult the current pf.conf(5), including match, nat-to,
rdr-to and queue syntax, rather than applying the old examples unchanged.
